  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{7,14,21},{28,35,42,\u2026,84},{91,98,105,\u2026,154}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{7,14,21,\u2026,154}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{7,14,21,28,35},{42,49,56,63,70}}$ is not a partition because the elements $77,84,\u2026,154$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{7,14,21,28,35,42,\u2026,77},{91,98},{105,112,119,\u2026,154}}$ is not a partition because the element $84$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{7,14,21,\u2026,63},{56,63,70,\u2026,154}}$ is not a partition because the elements $56$ and $63$ appear in multiple subsets.",
